## Contracts

A change breaks the contract when it breaks any of:

{{contract_list}}

## When to bump

| Bump | When | Example in this workspace |
|---|---|---|
| PATCH | Fixes, security patches, performance without behavior change; no new feature | {{patch_example}} |
| MINOR | At least one new backward-compatible feature (screens, endpoints, optional fields, additive migrations, config with defaults, deprecations); PATCH resets | {{minor_example}} |
| MAJOR | Any contract break: removed or renamed endpoint/field, changed meaning, required config without default, a migration that breaks the running version, forced mobile update, permission model change | {{major_example}} |

The highest impact in the release wins. A business-driven MAJOR needs a recorded, approved decision.

## Computing it

From commits since the last tag: `feat` → MINOR, `fix`/`perf` → PATCH, `!`/`BREAKING CHANGE` → MAJOR. The agent proposes the version with the commit list, AC and reason; {{release_approver}} approves.

