## Single source of truth

Tag first; files `{{version_files}}` are synced by `{{version_sync_cmd}}`. {{mobile_build_note}} Changelog groups: Added / Changed / Fixed / Security, written for users.

## Releasing to production (the user runs it)

The agent prepares this checklist and the commands; it never runs the merge, the tag or the deploy.

1. STG passed for `{{release_pattern}}` @ `<sha>`.
2. R1: every hotfix on `{{production_branch}}` is in the release — `git log --oneline origin/<release>..origin/{{production_branch}}` is empty (or only merge commits already contained).
3. Merge the release into `{{production_branch}}` (merge commit).
4. R2: `git diff origin/<release> <merge-commit>` is empty; otherwise test again on STG.
5. Tag `{{tag_format}}` with the release SHA in the message; promote the tested artifact `<registry>/<app>:<sha>`.
6. Propagate as [04]({{ref_04}}) requires; delete the release branch when done.

